<title>NETHERLANDS: BOLSWESSANEN SEES NO TAKEOVER BID.</title>
<headline>BOLSWESSANEN SEES NO TAKEOVER BID.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch food and drinks group BolsWessanen NV said on Wednesday it had no indication that it would be subject to a takeover bid.  </p>
<p>&quot;Given spectulation in an English daily newspaper ... about a possible takeover of Koninklijke BolsWessanen NV we announce that we do not have any indications of this (takeover bid),&quot; BolsWessanen said in a brief statement.</p>
<p>Prior to the announcement, its shares were suspended on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange for 15 minutes until 10.45 GMT.</p>
<p>Before the suspension the shares gained 1.60 at 30.20 guilders on talk that British drinks group Grand Metropolitan was angling for a takeover of BolsWessanen. Trading group Hagemeyer was also rumoured to be interested.</p>
